WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.760
So it's very quickly getting very real in
the impeachment inquiry against Donald Trump.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.160
This is starting to now I'll

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:12.539
get into, people are going to have to show
up, people are going to have to provide documents

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:14.999
or maybe face the consequences of not doing
so.

00:00:14.999 --> 00:00:20.880
Although it's not totally clear in this administration
if there will be ever consequences for ignoring

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.900
subpoenas and the latest person subpoenaed
as Rudy Donald Trump's personal lawyer, Rudy

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:31.110
Giuliani, who has been subpoenaed by the house
intelligence committee to provide a number

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:35.710
of different documents and Rudy of course,
is one of the sort of top people who's been

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:44.649
involved in this campaign to pressure Ukraine
into helping Donald Trump in 2020 by investigating,

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:50.420
which is of course of course code for investigate
and determine that you as a result of that

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.670
investigation need to say negative things
about Joe Biden.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:01:00.660
The letter to Rudy Giuliani identifies him
as an agent of Trump in the scheme to advance

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:07.100
Trump's interests through abuses of power
and they want documents from Rudy and I don't

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.500
know that they're going to get documents from
Rudy.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:15.200
This is an administration that has gotten
away with simply ignoring subpoenas and subpoena

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.900
power, although not uncontroversial.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:23.950
I mean, listen, there are reasonable debates
you can have about edge cases or blurry area

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.130
cases with regard to subpoena power.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:31.170
Can subpoena power be abused, you know, with
any mechanism.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:36.869
There are debates to be had, but this is an
administration that has just directly and,

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:43.970
and unabashedly flouted a subpoena power,
ignoring all sorts of requests for everything

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:48.580
from Donald Trump business records that could
be tied to a mall, humans clause violations

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:53.410
or potential money laundering all the way
up through and including requests, subpoena

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:59.490
requests for, um, witnesses to show up and
talk about possible crimes that they have

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:00.490
witnessed.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:07.130
So I hope that subpoenas that are apart of
an impeachment inquiry will not be allowed

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.280
to be ignored.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:13.300
But I don't know the answer to that because
the precedent under this administration has

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.250
been that they just ignore them and then there
are no consequences.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:23.010
Now we've also learned in the last 24 hours
that the secretary of state, Mike Palm PEO

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:28.630
was also listening in on live on that phone
call on July 25th between Donald Trump and

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.000
the Ukrainian president.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.420
We didn't previously know that prior to, you
know, 12 or 16 hours ago and Palm PEO himself

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.590
is becoming a bigger and bigger part of this
entire impeachment inquiry.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:46.090
And what we are seeing if we zoom out a little
bit, is that this is growing into one of the

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:52.580
most sort of all encompassing political scandals
for an administration and a long time.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:57.290
And I think that it actually is informative
to compare and contrast to the impeachment

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:02.340
of bill Clinton because a lot of people on
the ripe love to bring up bill Clinton in

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.590
the context of Trump's wrongdoing and impeachment
as they look.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:06.590
Clinton got impeached.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.090
Uh, let's go back to bill Clinton's impeachment.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:13.370
Bill Clinton was impeached for lying about
an affair.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.580
Bill Clinton cooperated.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.920
Bill Clinton did not attempt to tamper with
witnesses.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.940
He didn't attempt to obstruct the process
of investigation.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.740
He didn't ignore subpoenas.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.769
His attorney wasn't part of the scandal.

00:03:26.769 --> 00:03:29.220
His secretary of state wasn't part of the
scandal.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:34.239
His attorney general wasn't part of the scandal
and this is one of the major differences here

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:36.870
that we see with what's happening with Donald
Trump.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.250
It's not just Trump did a thing.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.920
First of all, the thing Trump did is really
bad.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.440
It's way worse than lying about an affair.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.000
It's pressuring.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.409
Pressuring is not even a heavy enough word,
but it's extorting a foreign power to smear

00:03:52.409 --> 00:03:54.209
a possible election opponent.

00:03:54.209 --> 00:04:00.340
That's number one, but Trump's lawyer, former
New York city mayor Rudy Giuliani is involved.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.019
His attorney general William Barr is involved.

00:04:03.019 --> 00:04:09.489
His secretary of state, Mike Palm PEO is involved
documents related to the incident.

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:14.569
In this case, a full transcript of the phone
call on July 25th with the Ukrainian president

00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:18.979
has been moved from the place where it would
normally be kept to some other place in order

00:04:18.979 --> 00:04:21.259
to obscure and obfuscate.

00:04:21.259 --> 00:04:24.779
So anyone even remotely comparing this to
the Clinton impeachment.

00:04:24.779 --> 00:04:26.719
I welcome that comparison.

00:04:26.719 --> 00:04:30.139
If you think that there's anything similar
about the two situations, you don't understand

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:35.849
the facts or you're deliberately ignoring
them, but that then gets us to the real sort

00:04:35.849 --> 00:04:43.999
of important pressing question, which is what
does happen if Rudy Giuliani ignores the subpoena?

00:04:43.999 --> 00:04:45.310
Can you imagine that?

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.990
I mean, just think back to the immediately
post nine 11 days.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:55.379
At one point, Rudy Giuliani was a widely respected
politician in the United States, even by many

00:04:55.379 --> 00:04:56.379
Democrats.

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:57.520
Now I want to be very clear.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.199
Uh, many of those Democrats disagreed with
the policies of Rudy Giuliani in New York

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:05.669
city, for example, broken windows, policing
and so on.

00:05:05.669 --> 00:05:12.360
But in a very general sense, to the extent
that you see bi-partisan, not support, but

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.470
at least recognition that someone is a good
faith actor.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:20.789
Rudy Giuliani was one of those people for
a period of time in the United States.

00:05:20.789 --> 00:05:26.659
Then he became mayor nine 11 where any question
he was asked politically was, you remember

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.300
I was mayor during nine 11.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.300
Right?

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:35.599
And now he has become Trump's hatchet man
involved in who knows how many possible crimes

00:05:35.599 --> 00:05:42.599
involved as maybe the most irrational, reflexive
defender of anything that Donald Trump does

00:05:42.599 --> 00:05:45.339
or says always all the time.

00:05:45.339 --> 00:05:47.319
And there's some sad element to it.

00:05:47.319 --> 00:05:51.809
I read some commentaries online saying it's
actually sad what's happened to Rudy Giuliani.

00:05:51.809 --> 00:05:53.539
Uh, he chose us.

00:05:53.539 --> 00:05:54.539
He chose this.

00:05:54.539 --> 00:05:58.879
So I don't feel bad for the guy, but it is
interesting to look at just how far he has

00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:04.569
fallen from being a, a man, an American political
character that at one point at least had the

00:06:04.569 --> 00:06:09.589
respect, if not support of people on the other
side of the political aisle.

00:06:09.589 --> 00:06:11.389
We will see what happens as far as the Rudy
Rudy Giuliani subpoena.

